    <briefdescription>
<para>Production implementation of <computeroutput>ingestion::ITensorDecompositionBackend</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Wraps <computeroutput>storage::TensorTrainDecomposer</computeroutput> and performs:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>κ-gate</bold> (<computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_ingestion_bridge_1ace1140241b22d7ba0d9e2a649ad4e5d7" kindref="member">shouldDecompose</ref></computeroutput>) — cheap pilot decomposition to check whether the data is worth compressing.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Mode-shape inference</bold> — an embedding of length <computeroutput>d</computeroutput> is reshaped into a 2D tensor (√d × √d when d is a perfect square, otherwise into a pair of factors maximally balanced in size). This gives order-2 TT-cores which are mathematically equivalent to the AdaLoRA SVD format (see <computeroutput>ADALORA_TT_BRIDGE_RESEARCH.md §2.3</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Provenance</bold> — the resulting <computeroutput>TensorCoreRecord</computeroutput> metadata includes <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>max_rank</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>mode_shape</computeroutput> to allow faithful reconstruction and auditing by downstream consumers (FITKO, eJustice). </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
